'''Pons Ora''' was one of the few [[City|settlements]] on the surface of [[Abafar]], a remote [[desert]] [[Planet|world]] located in the [[Outer Rim Territories]], and served as the planet's de facto seat of government. During the [[Clone Wars]], it was host to a [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[rhydonium]] [[Rhydonium mining installation|mining installation]].

==History==
===Clone Wars===
During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] used Pons Ora's [[Rhydonium mining installation|mining installation]] to mine for rhydonium,<ref name="SWE">{{SWE|locations|abafar|Abafar}}</ref> which had otherwise largely been mined out on the [[planet]] [[Abafar]].<ref name="Missing in Action" />

After the [[Battle of Sarrish]], a devastating loss for the [[Galactic Republic]], [[clone commando]] [[Clone Captain|Captain]] [[Gregor]], a survivor of the battle, wound up on Abafar with [[amnesia]]. He was found by the [[Sullustan]] [[Borkus]], a resident of Pons Ora, who, although realizing that Gregor was a soldier, manipulated him into working as a dishwasher at his diner [[Power Sliders]] for low wages as he did not know who he was.<ref name="Missing in Action" />

Later in the war, the [[D-Squad]], a special Republic unit consisting mostly of [[droid]]s, crash-landed on Abafar on their way back from a [[Mission to steal a Separatist encryption module|mission]] to steal a Separatist [[encryption module]]. After wandering through [[the Void]] for some time, all the members of the unit eventually made it to Pons Ora, with the [[astromech droid]]s, led by [[R2-D2]], reaching the city long before [[Zilkin]] [[Colonel]] [[Meebur Gascon]] and [[DUM-series pit droid]] [[WAC-47]].<ref name="Sunny Day in the Void" /> After regrouping, Gascon sent the astromechs to scout the town, while he went to get food for himself. Gascon chose the Power Sliders diner, but he and WAC were chased out by Borkus after he loudly announced himself as a Republic officer, in part because Borkus did not want them to see Gregor. However, at WAC's suggestion, Gascon went around to the back to dumpster-dive for food and encountered the amnesiac [[Cloning|clone]] anyways, who was deeply confused by the duo's insistence that he was a soldier.<ref name="Missing in Action" />

===Imperial era===
By the [[time]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], the [[Sullustan]] [[Mun Liiv]] served as [[Governor]] of Abafar, a position instated by the Empire. Liiv led a [[Abafar mining confederation|confederation]] of the planet's largest rhydonium mines, including the [[Pons Ora refinery|refinery]] at Pons Ora which was the planet's largest. From Pons Ora, Liiv coordinated deliveries from the city's small spaceport from other mining communities on the planet. Despite Liiv's status as governor of the planet, the Empire had a limited presence on or near Abafar, with Imperial [[starship]]s only entering the [[Abafar system|system]] to retrieve rhydonium.<ref name="FiB" />

